# INT-SOURCE: ../functional/117_box_in_struct_array.my
# INT-ENGINES: tw default nj noopt
#
# INT unit (#107): a box<P> is never packed into a flat array of P
# values. The functional program runs as a coverage unit too, under the
# engines above, with no second copy (INT-SOURCE); it asserts its own
# results and every engine must print the same. It owns the refusals of
# a store and an append of a box into a flat array<P> through a `dyn`
# name, which no other unit reaches.
